//dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-camp-closure-flash-report-gubio-camp-borno-state-22-december-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NE%20-%20Gubio%20Camp%20Relocation%20Konduga%20LGA%20%28Borno%20State%29%2022%20December%202022.pdf", "summary": "As part of the IDP relocation programme issued by the Borno State Government (BSG), the 400 Housing Estate Camp (or Gubio Camp), located in the Ward Auno Chabbol of Konduga LGA, was closed between December 1, 2022, and December 10, 2022.", "matched_on": "title:camp closure", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-12-22", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 697, "title": "Nigeria — North-central & North-west Flash Report #128 (20 December 2022)", "date": "2022-12-22", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flash", "component": "Incident / Flash Report", "regions": ["North Central", "North West"], "states": ["Kaduna"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-north-central-north-west-flash-report-128-20-december-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NCNW%20128%20%2820%20December%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "On 18 December, clashes between herders and farmers were reported in the Malagum community of Malagum ward and the community Sakong village of Kpak ward, both located in Kaura LGA of Kaduna State. The clashes affected 2,984 individuals, who remained in the communities. As a result of the clashes, 40 fatalities and 4 injuries were reported.", "matched_on": "title:flash report", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-12-20", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 698, "title": "Nigeria — Emergency Tracking Tool Report 306 (12 - 18 December 2022)", "date": "2022-12-22", "year": 2022, "component_key": "ett", "component": "Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT)", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Adamawa", "Borno"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-emergency-tracking-tool-report-306-12-18-december-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Emergency%20Tracking%20Tool%20%28ETT%29%20Report%20No.%20306.pdf", "summary": "The DTM Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT) is deployed to track and to collect information on large and sudden population, provide frequent updates on the scale of displacement and quantify the affected population when needed. As a sub-component of the Mobility Tracking methodology in Nigeria, ETT utilises direct observation and a broad network of key informants to capture best estimates of the affected population per location, enabling targeted humanitarian response planning. Between 12 and 18 December 2022, a total of 3,123 new arrivals were recorded in locations in Adamawa and Borno States. The ", "matched_on": "title:emergency tracking tool", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-12-18", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 699, "title": "Nigeria — Flood Rapid Needs Assessment Dashboard — Plateau State (25 November 2022)", "date": "2022-12-19", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flood", "component": "Post-Flood Situation Report (Ad-Hoc)", "regions": ["North Central"], "states": ["Plateau"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-flood-rapid-needs-assessment-dashboard-plateau-state-25-november-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigera%20DTM%20Flood%20Response%20Report%20NC%20-%20Plateau%20State%20%2829%20November%202022%29%20V2.pdf", "summary": "The rainy season in Nigeria typically occurs annually with the greatest concentration of precipitation between the months of June and September. Many states in Nigeria have been aﬀected by unprecedented heavy rainfalls and floods have devastated various communities. Infrastructure, crops, and shelters have been damaged which led to decimated livelihoods and the displacement of numerous households. Between 28 October and 1 November 2022, DTM, in collaboration with the National Emergency Management Agency (NEMA), the Plateau State Emergency Management Agency (SEMA) and the Nigerian Red Cross Soc", "matched_on": "title:flood rapid needs", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-11-25", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 700, "title": "Nigeria — Flood Rapid Needs Assessment Dashboard — Katsina State (24 November 2022)", "date": "2022-12-19", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flood", "component": "Post-Flood Situation Report (Ad-Hoc)", "regions": ["North West"], "states": ["Katsina"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-flood-rapid-needs-assessment-dashboard-katsina-state-24-november-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flood%20Report%20NW%20-%20Katsina%20State%20%2824%20November%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "The rainy season in Nigeria typically occurs annually with the greatest concentration of precipitation between the months of June and September. Many states in Nigeria have been aﬀected by unprecedented heavy rainfalls and floods have devastated various communities. Infrastructure, crops, and shelters have been damaged which led to decimated livelihoods and the displacement of numerous households. Over the past months, climate variability and the release of excess water from the Lagdo dam in northern Cameroon, have worsened the flood situation and has resulted in a renewed situation of widespr", "matched_on": "title:flood rapid needs", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-11-24", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 701, "title": "Nigeria — Flood Rapid Needs Assessment Dashboard — Kano State (18 November 2022)", "date": "2022-12-19", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flood", "component": "Post-Flood Situation Report (Ad-Hoc)", "regions": ["North West"], "states": ["Kano"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-flood-rapid-needs-assessment-dashboard-kano-state-18-november-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flood%20Report%20NW-Kano%20State%20%2822%20November%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "The rainy season in Nigeria typically occurs annually with the greatest concentration of precipitation between the months of June and September. Many states in Nigeria have been aﬀected by unprecedented heavy rainfalls and floods have devastated various communities. Infrastructure, crops, and shelters have been damaged which led to decimated livelihoods and the displacement of numerous households. Over the past months, climate variability and the release of excess water from the Lagdo dam in northern Cameroon, have worsened the flood situation and has resulted in a renewed situation of widespr", "matched_on": "title:flood rapid needs", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-11-18", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 702, "title": "Nigeria — Flood Rapid Needs Assessment Dashboard — Kaduna State (28 November 2022)", "date": "2022-12-19", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flood", "component": "Post-Flood Situation Report (Ad-Hoc)", "regions": ["North West"], "states": ["Kaduna"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-flood-rapid-needs-assessment-dashboard-kaduna-state-28-november-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20Flood%20Report%20NW%20-Kaduna%20state%20%2825%20November%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "The rainy season in Nigeria typically occurs annually with the greatest concentration of precipitation between the months of June and September. Many states in Nigeria have been aﬀected by unprecedented heavy rainfalls and floods have devastated various communities. Infrastructure, crops, and shelters have been damaged which led to decimated livelihoods and the displacement of numerous households. Over the past months, climate variability and the release of excess water from the overflow of river Kaduna, have worsened the flood situation and has resulted in a renewed situation of widespread di", "matched_on": "title:flood rapid needs", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-11-28", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 703, "title": "Nigeria — Flood Rapid Needs Assessment Dashboard — Borno State (25 November 2022)", "date": "2022-12-19", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flood", "component": "Post-Flood Situation Report (Ad-Hoc)", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Borno"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-flood-rapid-needs-assessment-dashboard-borno-state-25-november-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flood%20Report%20NE%20-%20Borno%20State%20%2021%20November%202022%20V3.pdf", "summary": "The rainy season in Nigeria typically occurs annually with the greatest concentration of precipitation between the months of June and September. Many states in Nigeria have been aﬀected by unprecedented heavy rainfalls and floods have devastated various communities. Infrastructure, crops, and shelters have been damaged which led to decimated livelihoods and the displacement of numerous households. Over the past months, climate variability and the release of excess water from the Lagdo dam in northern Cameroon, have worsened the flood situation and has resulted in a renewed situation of widespr", "matched_on": "title:flood rapid needs", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-11-25", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 704, "title": "Nigeria — Flood Rapid Needs Assessment Dashboard — Bauchi State (28 November 2022)", "date": "2022-12-19", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flood", "component": "Post-Flood Situation Report (Ad-Hoc)", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Bauchi"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-flood-rapid-needs-assessment-dashboard-bauchi-state-28-november-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flood%20Report%20NE-Bauchi%20State%20%2818%20November%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "The rainy season in Nigeria typically occurs annually with the greatest concentration of precipitation between the months of June and September. Many states in Nigeria have been aﬀected by unprecedented heavy rainfalls and floods have devastated various communities. Infrastructure, crops, and shelters have been damaged which led to decimated livelihoods and the displacement of numerous households. Over the past months, climate variability and the release of excess water from the Lagdo dam in northern Cameroon, have worsened the flood situation and has resulted in a renewed situation of widespr", "matched_on": "title:flood rapid needs", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-11-28", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 705, "title": "Nigeria — Emergency Tracking Tool Report 305 (05 - 11 December 2022)", "date": "2022-12-16", "year": 2022, "component_key": "ett", "component": "Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT)", "regions": [], "states": [], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-emergency-tracking-tool-report-305-05-11-december-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Emergency%20Tracking%20Tool%20%28ETT%29%20Report%20No.%20305.pdf", "summary": "The DTM Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT) is deployed to track and to collect information on large and sudden population and sudden population movements, provide frequent updates on the scale of displacement and quantify the aﬀected population when needed. As a sub-component of the Mobility Tracking methodology in Nigeria, ETT utilises direct observation and a broad network of key informants to capture best estimates of the aﬀected population per location, enabling targeted humanitarian response planning. Between 05 and 11 December 2022, a total of 1,262 new arrivals were recorded in locations in ", "matched_on": "title:emergency tracking tool", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-12-11", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 706, "title": "Nigeria — North-central & North-west Flash Report #127 (13 December 2022)", "date": "2022-12-15", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flash", "component": "Incident / Flash Report", "regions": ["North Central", "North West"], "states": ["Katsina"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-north-central-north-west-flash-report-127-13-december-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NCNW%20127%20%2813%20December%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "On 06 December, armed bandits reportedly attacked the communities Daurawa and Garin Ajiya in Wagini ward of Batsari LGA in Katsina State. The attack affected 952 individuals and led to the displacement of 494 individuals in Garin Ajiya to the community Unguwar Gwanda Sabon Gari in Batsari ward, while those affected in Daurawa remained in the community. As a result of the attacks, 6 fatalities and 24 injuries were reported.", "matched_on": "title:flash report", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-12-13", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 707, "title": "Nigeria — North-central & North-west Flash Report #126 (6 December 2022)", "date": "2022-12-09", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flash", "component": "Incident / Flash Report", "regions": ["North Central", "North West"], "states": ["Katsina"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-north-central-north-west-flash-report-126-6-december-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NCNW%20126%20%286%20December%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "On 04 December, armed bandits reportedly attacked the community Karare in Karare ward of Batsari LGA in Katsina State. The attack affected 398 individuals, who remianed in the community. As a result of the attack, one fatality and 43 injuries were reported.", "matched_on": "title:flash report", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-12-06", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 708, "title": "Nigeria — North-central & North-west Flash Report #125 (29 November 2022)", "date": "2022-12-09", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flash", "component": "Incident / Flash Report", "regions": ["North Central", "North West"], "states": ["Zamfara"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-north-central-north-west-flash-report-125-29-november-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NCNW%20125%20%2829%20November%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "On 21 November, armed bandits reportedly attacked the community Gidan Goga in Gidan Goga ward of Maradun LGA in Zamfara State. The attack affected 2,810 individuals and displaced 2,808 individuals to the community Sarki Baura/Sarki Mafara in Kaura Namoda LGA. As a result of the attack, 2 fatalities and 5 injuries were reported.", "matched_on": "title:flash report", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-11-29", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 709, "title": "Nigeria — North-central & North-west Flash Report #124 (15 November 2022)", "date": "2022-12-09", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flash", "component": "Incident / Flash Report", "regions": ["North Central", "North West"], "states": ["Benue", "Plateau"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-north-central-north-west-flash-report-124-15-november-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NCNW%20124%20%2822%20November%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "On 14 November, a clash between herders and farmers was reported in the Zaki Biam community of Uyam ward in Ukum LGA, Benue State. The attack affected 45 individuals who currently are given shelter by neighbours within the community.  As a result of the attack, 1 fatality and 6 injuries were reported. On 15 November, a clash between herders and farmers was reported in the Mai Katako community of Butura ward in Bokkos LGA, Plateau State. The attack affected 756 individuals, who remained in the community.  As a result of the attack, 12 fatalities and 7 injuries were reported. On 17 November in B", "matched_on": "title:flash report", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-11-15", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 710, "title": "Nigeria — Emergency Tracking Tool Report 304 (28 November - 04 December 2022)", "date": "2022-12-09", "year": 2022, "component_key": "ett", "component": "Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT)", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Adamawa"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-emergency-tracking-tool-report-304-28-november-04-december-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Emergency%20Tracking%20Tool%20%28ETT%29%20Report%20No.%20304.pdf", "summary": "The DTM Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT) is deployed to track and to collect information on large and sudden population movements, provide frequent updates on the scale of displacement and quantify the aﬀected population when needed. As a sub-component of the Mobility Tracking methodology in Nigeria, ETT utilises direct observation and a broad network of key informants to capture best estimates of the aﬀected population per location, enabling targeted humanitarian response planning. Between 28 November and 04 December 2022, a total of 1,424 new arrivals were recorded in locations in Adamawa and B", "matched_on": "title:emergency tracking tool", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-12-04", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 711, "title": "Nigeria — COVID-19 Point of Entry Monthly Dashboard (October 2022)", "date": "2022-12-09", "year": 2022, "component_key": "poe", "component": "Point of Entry (POE) Reports", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Borno"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-covid-19-point-entry-monthly-dashboard-october-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20COVID-19%20Point%20of%20Entry%20Dashboard%20%28October%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "During the COVID-19 pandemic, IOM's Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM), in collaboration with the World Health Organization (WHO), monitors cross-border movements to and from Nigeria's Borno State in north-east Nigeria. Assessments are conducted at Points of Entry located along the border with Cameroon.", "matched_on": "title:point of entry", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-10-01", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 712, "title": "Nigeria — Transhumance Tracking Tool Report — Early Warning Dashboard 11 (November 2022)", "date": "2022-12-08", "year": 2022, "component_key": "ewer", "component": "Early Warning & Early Response Dashboard", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Adamawa"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-transhumance-tracking-tool-report-early-warning-dashboard-11-november-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/Nigeria%20%E2%80%94%20Transhumance%20Tracking%20Tool%20Report%20%E2%80%94%20Early%20Warning%20Dashboard%2011%20%28November%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "As a component of the IOM's Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM), the Transhumance Tracking Tool (TTT) Early Warning System, with support from community focal points and key informants, collects information on alerts relating to transhumance activities and movements in 5 Local Government Areas in Adamawa State (Demsa, Girei, Lamurde, Numan and Mayo-Belwa). During this period, 248 alerts were recorded. These alerts consist of 230 events (93%) and 18 movements (7%). The reported events are instances that are related to agro-pastoral conflicts, inter and inter-community tensions, violent clashes, k", "matched_on": "title:early warning dashboard", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-11-01", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 713, "title": "Nigeria — Fire Outbreak Flash Report — Borno State (7 December 2022)", "date": "2022-12-08", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flash", "component": "Incident / Flash Report", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Borno"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-fire-outbreak-flash-report-borno-state-7-december-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NE%20-%20Ajiri%20fire%20outbreak%2C%20Mafa%20LGA%2C%20Borno%20State%20%2807%20December%202022%29%20%283%29.pdf", "summary": "On 29 November 2022, a fire outbreak was reported at Ajiri a host community location in Mafa LGA of Borno State. The fire damaged and destroyed shelters and belongings of numerous IDP households. Ajiri is one of the communities where IDPs from Farm Center Camp  and Custom House 2 Camp (which were closed in September 2021) were relocated to by the state government. The fire incident destroyed 157 emergency shelters, aﬀecting a total of 826 individuals in 156 households. The aﬀected individuals included 435 children, 217 women and 172 men.", "matched_on": "title:flash report", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-12-07", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 714, "title": "Nigeria — Emergency Tracking Tool Report 303 (21 - 27 November 2022)", "date": "2022-12-02", "year": 2022, "component_key": "ett", "component": "Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT)", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Adamawa", "Borno"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-emergency-tracking-tool-report-303-21-27-november-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Emergency%20Tracking%20Tool%20%28ETT%29%20Report%20No.%20303%20%2821%20-%2027%20November%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "The DTM Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT) is deployed to track and to collect information on large and sudden population movements, provide frequent updates on the scale of displacement and quantify the aﬀected population when needed. As a sub-component of the Mobility Tracking methodology in Nigeria, ETT utilises direct observation and a broad network of key informants to capture best estimates of the aﬀected population per location, enabling targeted humanitarian response planning. Between 21 and 27 November 2022, a total of 1,358 new arrivals were recorded in locations in Adamawa and Borno Stat", "matched_on": "title:emergency tracking tool", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-11-27", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 715, "title": "Nigeria — North-central & North-west Flash Report #123 (15 November 2022)", "date": "2022-12-01", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flash", "component": "Incident / Flash Report", "regions": ["North Central", "North West"], "states": ["Zamfara"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-north-central-north-west-flash-report-123-15-november-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NCNW%20123%20%2814%20November%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "On 07 November, armed bandits reportedly attacked the communities Kwangami in Galadima/Yan Ruwa ward of Zurmi LGA, Kadauda/Gangade in Wanke ward of Gusau, Masu in Bukkuyum ward of Bukkuyum LGA and Waramu in Waramu ward of Anka LGA. All mentioned LGAs are situated in the state of Zamfara. The attacks affected a total of 1,889 individuals, who remained in their respective communities. As a result of the attacks, 7 fatalities and 27 injuries were reported.", "matched_on": "title:flash report", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-11-15", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 716, "title": "Nigeria — Emergency Tracking Tool Report 302 (14 - 20 November 2022)", "date": "2022-11-25", "year": 2022, "component_key": "ett", "component": "Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT)", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Adamawa", "Borno"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-emergency-tracking-tool-report-302-14-20-november-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Emergency%20Tracking%20Tool%20%28ETT%29%20Report%20No.%20302..pdf", "summary": "The DTM Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT) is deployed to track and to collect information on large and sudden population movements, provide frequent updates on the scale of displacement and quantify the aﬀected population when needed. As a sub-component of the Mobility Tracking methodology in Nigeria, ETT utilises direct observation and a broad network of key informants to capture best estimates of the aﬀected population per location, enabling targeted humanitarian response planning. Between 14 and 20 November 2022, a total of 1,469 new arrivals were recorded in locations in Adamawa, Borno and Yob", "matched_on": "title:emergency tracking tool", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-11-20", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 717, "title": "Nigeria — Flow Monitoring Dashboard 56 (August 2022)", "date": "2022-11-24", "year": 2022, "component_key": "fmp", "component": "Flow Monitoring (migrants) – extra category", "regions": ["North Central", "North West"], "states": ["Nasarawa", "Niger", "Kano", "Sokoto"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-flow-monitoring-dashboard-56-august-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/Flow%20Monitoring%20Dashboard%2056%20August%202022_0.pdf", "summary": "In Nigeria, DTM conducts Flow Monitoring activities in several important transit locations in Sokoto and Kano to monitor the movements of passenger buses to and from Niger. The Sokoto FMPs covers three migratory routes in Illela, Gada and Sabon- Birnin . And the Kano FMPs ( Kofar Ruwa Park and Yankaba Park) covers two migratory routes in Dala and Nasarawa Local Government Areas in Kano state. This report presents data collected on flows, routes, provenance, destination and demographic profiles of travellers observed at the FMPs in August 2022 .", "matched_on": "title:flow monitoring", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-08-01", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 718, "title": "Nigeria — Emergency Tracking Tool Report 301 (07 - 13 November 2022)", "date": "2022-11-18", "year": 2022, "component_key": "ett", "component": "Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT)", "regions": [], "states": [], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-emergency-tracking-tool-report-301-07-13-november-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Emergency%20Tracking%20Tool%20%28ETT%29%20Report%20No.%20301.pdf", "summary": "The DTM Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT) is deployed to track and to collect information on large and sudden population movements, provide frequent updates on the scale of displacement and quantify the affected population when needed. As a sub-component of the Mobility Tracking methodology in Nigeria, ETT utilises direct observation and a broad network of key informants to capture best estimates of the affected population per location, enabling targeted humanitarian response planning.", "matched_on": "title:emergency tracking tool", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-11-13", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 719, "title": "Nigeria — Flood Rapid Needs Assessment Dashboard — Kogi State (15 November 2022)", "date": "2022-11-15", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flood", "component": "Post-Flood Situation Report (Ad-Hoc)", "regions": ["North Central"], "states": ["Kogi"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-flood-rapid-needs-assessment-dashboard-kogi-state-15-november-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flood%20Report%20-%20Kogi%20State%20%2823%20November%202022%29_0.pdf", "summary": "The rainy season in Nigeria typically occurs annually with the greatest concentration of precipitation between the months of June and September. Many states in Nigeria have been aﬀected by unprecedented heavy rainfalls and floods have devastated various communities. Infrastructure, crops, and shelters have been damaged which led to decimated livelihoods and the displacement of numerous households. Over the past months, climate variability and the release of excess water from the Lagdo dam in northern Cameroon, have worsened the flood situation and has resulted in a renewed situation of widespr", "matched_on": "title:flood rapid needs", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-11-15", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 720, "title": "Nigeria — Transhumance Tracking Tool Report — Early Warning Dashboard 10 (October 2022)", "date": "2022-11-14", "year": 2022, "component_key": "ewer", "component": "Early Warning & Early Response Dashboard", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Adamawa"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-transhumance-tracking-tool-report-early-warning-dashboard-10-october-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/Nigeria%20%E2%80%94%20Transhumance%20Tracking%20Tool%20Report%20%E2%80%94%20Early%20Warning%20Dashboard%2010%20%28October%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "Early Warning System of Transhumance Tracking Tool (TTT) as a component of the IOM's Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM) aided by community Key Informants record through the focal person, related alerts to transhumance activities. This report presents TTT Early Warning alerts collected in five LGAs of Adamawa State (Demsa, Girei, Lamurde, Numan and Mayo-Belwa) for October 2022. 214 alerts were recorded for the period under review, including 203 events and 11 movement alerts that represent 95 and 5 per cent of alerts, respectively. Lamurde LGA recorded the highest number of alerts at 26 per cent", "matched_on": "title:early warning dashboard", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-10-01", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 721, "title": "Nigeria — North-central & North-west Flash Report #122 (9 November 2022)", "date": "2022-11-11", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flash", "component": "Incident / Flash Report", "regions": ["North Central", "North West"], "states": ["Benue"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-north-central-north-west-flash-report-122-9-november-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NCNW%20122%20%287%20November%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "On 3rd of November, armed bandits reportedly attacked the communities Udar Yagba and Ukohol in Nyiev ward of Guma LGA in Benue State. The attacks aﬀected 837 individuals, who were displaced to the communities Ortesy in Nyiev ward and Ndzorov in Ndzorov Council ward. As a result of the attacks, 15 fatalities and 36 injuries were reported.", "matched_on": "title:flash report", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-11-09", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 722, "title": "Nigeria — Emergency Tracking Tool Report 300 (31 October - 6 November 2022)", "date": "2022-11-11", "year": 2022, "component_key": "ett", "component": "Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT)", "regions": [], "states": [], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-emergency-tracking-tool-report-300-31-october-6-november-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Emergency%20Tracking%20Tool%20%28ETT%29%20Report%20No.%20300%20.pdf", "summary": "The DTM Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT) is deployed to track and to collect information on large and sudden population movements, provide frequent updates on the scale of displacement and quantify the affected population when needed. As a sub-component of the Mobility Tracking methodology in Nigeria, ETT utilises direct observation and a broad network of key informants to capture best estimates of the affected population per location, enabling targeted humanitarian response planning.", "matched_on": "title:emergency tracking tool", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-11-06", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 723, "title": "Nigeria — Flood Rapid Needs Assessment Dashboard — Anambra State (8 November 2022)", "date": "2022-11-09", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flood", "component": "Post-Flood Situation Report (Ad-Hoc)", "regions": ["South East"], "states": ["Anambra"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-flood-rapid-needs-assessment-dashboard-anambra-state-8-november-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/Anambra%20Flood%20Assessment%20Dashboard%20%289%20November%202022%29_3.pdf", "summary": "The rainy season in Nigeria typically occurs annually with the greatest concentration of precipitation between the months of June and September. Many states in Nigeria have been affected by unprecedented heavy rainfalls and floods have devastated various communities. Infrastructure, crops, and shelters have been damaged which led to decimated livelihoods and the displacement of numerous households. Over the past months, climate variability and the release of excess water from the Lagdo dam in northern Cameroon, have worsened the flood situation and has resulted in a renewed situation of widesp", "matched_on": "title:flood rapid needs", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-11-08", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 724, "title": "Nigeria — Emergency Tracking Tool Report 299 (24 - 30 October 2022)", "date": "2022-11-03", "year": 2022, "component_key": "ett", "component": "Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT)", "regions": [], "states": [], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-emergency-tracking-tool-report-299-24-30-october-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Emergency%20Tracking%20Tool%20%28ETT%29%20Report%20No.%20299.pdf", "summary": "The DTM Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT) is deployed to track and to collect information on large and sudden population movements, provide frequent updates on the scale of displacement and quantify the affected population when needed. As a sub-component of the Mobility Tracking methodology in Nigeria, ETT utilises direct observation and a broad network of key informants to capture best estimates of the affected population per location, enabling targeted humanitarian response planning.", "matched_on": "title:emergency tracking tool", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-10-30", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 725, "title": "Nigeria — North-Central and North-West — Mobility Tracking Round 10 IDP Atlas (October 2022)", "date": "2022-11-02", "year": 2022, "component_key": "atlas", "component": "Mobility Tracking – IDP & Returnee Atlas", "regions": ["North Central", "North West"], "states": [], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-north-central-and-north-west-mobility-tracking-round-10-idp-atlas-october-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IDP%20Atlas%20-%20NCNW%20R10%20updated.pdf", "summary": "IOM’s Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM) provides support to the Government and humanitarian partners by establishing a comprehensive system that collects, analyses and disseminates data on Internally Displaced Persons or IDPs to ensure timely and effective assistance to the affected populations. Data collection takes place at a granular level and is repeated at regular intervals to ensure accurate and up-to-date information. As of October 2022, the DTM identified a total of 1,087,875 IDPs in 180,307 households in Nigeria’s north-central and north-west zones. This signifies an IDP increase of ", "matched_on": "file name: IDP Atlas - NCNW R10 updated.pdf", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-10-01", "round": 10, "round_zone": "NCNW", "mt_main": true}, {"id": 726, "title": "Nigeria — Emergency Tracking Tool Report 298 (17 - 23 October 2022)", "date": "2022-10-28", "year": 2022, "component_key": "ett", "component": "Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT)", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Adamawa", "Borno"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-emergency-tracking-tool-report-298-17-23-october-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Emergency%20Tracking%20Tool%20%28ETT%29%20Report%20No.%20298.pdf", "summary": "The DTM Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT) is deployed to track and to collect information on large and sudden population movements, provide frequent updates on the scale of displacement and quantify the affected population when needed. As a sub-component of the Mobility Tracking methodology in Nigeria, ETT utilises direct observation and a broad network of key informants to capture best estimates of the affected population per location, enabling targeted humanitarian response planning. Between 17 and 23 October 2022, a total of 1,437 new arrivals were recorded in locations in Adamawa and Borno Sta", "matched_on": "title:emergency tracking tool", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-10-23", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 727, "title": "Nigeria — North-central & North-west Flash Report 121 (24 October 2022)", "date": "2022-10-27", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flash", "component": "Incident / Flash Report", "regions": ["North Central", "North West"], "states": ["Benue", "Zamfara"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-north-central-north-west-flash-report-121-24-october-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NCNW%20121%20%2824%20October%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "On 19 October, armed herders reportedly attacked the community Gbeji in the Ityuluv ward of Ukum LGA in Benue State. The attack aﬀected 305 individuals and displaced 254 individuals to Ayiin Camp in Mbagber ward of Logo LGA in Benue State. As a result of the attack, 51 fatalities and 26 injuries were reported. Also on 19 October, armed bandits reportedly attacked the community Unguwar Mata in Dangaladima ward of Anka LGA in Zamfara State. The attack aﬀected 735 individuals and displaced 732 individuals to New Emir Palace IDP Camp in Magaji ward of Anka LGA. As a result of the attack 3 fataliti", "matched_on": "title:flash report", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-10-24", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 728, "title": "Nigeria — Emergency Tracking Tool Quarterly Report (July - September 2022)", "date": "2022-10-24", "year": 2022, "component_key": "ett", "component": "Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT)", "regions": ["North East", "North Central"], "states": ["Adamawa", "Borno", "Yobe", "Niger"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-emergency-tracking-tool-quarterly-report-july-september-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Emergency%20Tracking%20Tool%20%28ETT%29%20Quarterly%20Report%20%20Jul%20-%20Sep%202022.pdf", "summary": "Between July and September 2022, a total of 41,650 new arrivals have been recorded at locations in Askira/Uba, Bama, Dikwa, Damboa, Gwoza, Hawul, Kala/Balge, Monguno and Ngala Local Government Areas (LGAs) of the most conflict-aﬀected Borno State; and in Demsa, Fufore, Girei, Gombi, 13Hong, Lamurde, Madagali, Maiha, Michika, Mubi North, Mubi South, Numan, Song, Yola North and Yola South LGAs of Adamawa State; and in Bade LGA of Yobe State. Out of the 41,650 arrivals, 3,215 individuals arrived from neighbouring countries (1,520 from Cameroon, 1,327 from the Republic of Niger and 368 from the Re", "matched_on": "title:emergency tracking tool", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-09-01", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 729, "title": "Nigeria — Flow Monitoring Dashboard 55 (July 2022)", "date": "2022-10-20", "year": 2022, "component_key": "fmp", "component": "Flow Monitoring (migrants) – extra category", "regions": ["North Central"], "states": ["Niger"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-flow-monitoring-dashboard-55-july-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/Flow%20Monitoring%20Dashboard%2055%20July%202022.pdf", "summary": "During the month of July 2022, a total of 31,510 migrants were observed at the various cross-border flow monitoring points (12,153 individuals entering Nigeria by the FMPs and 19,357 individuals leaving Nigeria by the FMPs). The average daily flow was 1,087, up by 6 per cent from the previous month. The increase in daily flow could be attributed to increased short-term commercial activities and movements as a result of seasonal farming along the Nigeria-Niger route. Many farmers are utilizing the rainy season for farming activities in rural areas of Nigeria and Niger. All observed travelers we", "matched_on": "title:flow monitoring", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-07-01", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 730, "title": "Nigeria — Emergency Tracking Tool Report 297 (10 - 16 October 2022)", "date": "2022-10-20", "year": 2022, "component_key": "ett", "component": "Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT)", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Adamawa", "Borno"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-emergency-tracking-tool-report-297-10-16-october-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Emergency%20Tracking%20Tool%20%28ETT%29%20Report%20No.%20297.pdf", "summary": "The DTM Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT) is deployed to track and to collect information on large and sudden population movements, provide frequent updates on the scale of displacement and quantify the aﬀected population when needed. As a sub-component of the Mobility Tracking methodology in Nigeria, ETT utilises direct observation and a broad network of key informants to capture best estimates of the aﬀected population per location, enabling targeted humanitarian response planning. Between 10 and 16 October 2022, a total of 1,413 new arrivals were recorded in locations in Adamawa and Borno State", "matched_on": "title:emergency tracking tool", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-10-16", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 731, "title": "Nigeria — North-central & North-west Flash Report 120 (17 October 2022)", "date": "2022-10-19", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flash", "component": "Incident / Flash Report", "regions": ["North Central", "North West"], "states": ["Benue", "Sokoto"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-north-central-north-west-flash-report-120-17-october-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NCNW%20120%20%2817%20October%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "On 10 October, armed bandits reportedly attacked the community Barkin Daji in the Kuruwa ward of Tureta LGA in Sokoto State. The attack aﬀected 94 individuals, who were displaced to the community of Kan Wuri in the Tureta ward of Tureta LGA. As a result of the attack, 2 injuries were reported. On 12 October, armed herders reportedly attacked the community of Yeluwata, located in Nyiev ward of Guma of Benue State. The attack aﬀected 199 individuals and led to the displacement of 193 individuals to the Ichwa Camp in North Bank I ward of Makurdi LGA in Benue state. As a result of the attack, 6 fa", "matched_on": "title:flash report", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-10-17", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 732, "title": "Nigeria — Transhumance Tracking Tool Report — Early Warning Dashboard 9 (September 2022)", "date": "2022-10-17", "year": 2022, "component_key": "ewer", "component": "Early Warning & Early Response Dashboard", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Adamawa"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-transhumance-tracking-tool-report-early-warning-dashboard-9-september-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/Nigeria%20%E2%80%94%20Transhumance%20Tracking%20Tool%20Report%20%E2%80%94%20Early%20Warning%20Dashboard%209%20%28September%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "A transhumance is a practice of pastoralism while sedentary farming activities are usually a method of agriculture in which the same land is farmed every year. Both practices represent two of the main ancestry and extensive economic activities within the West and Central Africa Sahel region. Traditionally, In Adamawa state, the farmers’ and herders’ livelihoods have complemented each other and the instance of conflicts was addressed by the established conflict resolution mechanisms and the traditional institutions. However, over the past few decades, a wide range of factors have resulted in te", "matched_on": "title:early warning dashboard", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-09-01", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 733, "title": "Nigeria — Emergency Tracking Tool Report 296 (03 - 09 October 2022)", "date": "2022-10-14", "year": 2022, "component_key": "ett", "component": "Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT)", "regions": [], "states": [], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-emergency-tracking-tool-report-296-03-09-october-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Emergency%20Tracking%20Tool%20%28ETT%29%20Report%20No.%20296.pdf", "summary": "The DTM Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT) is deployed to track and to collect information on large and sudden population movements, provide frequent updates on the scale of displacement and quantify the aﬀected population when needed. As a sub-component of the Mobility Tracking methodology in Nigeria, ETT utilises direct observation and a broad network of key informants to capture best estimates of the aﬀected population per location, enabling targeted humanitarian response planning.", "matched_on": "title:emergency tracking tool", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-10-09", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 734, "title": "Nigeria — North-central & North-west Flash Report 119 (10 October2022)", "date": "2022-10-12", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flash", "component": "Incident / Flash Report", "regions": ["North Central", "North West"], "states": ["Benue"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-north-central-north-west-flash-report-119-10-october2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NCNW%20119%20%2810%20October%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "On 04 and 06 October, armed herders reportedly attacked the communities Ityuluv in Ityuluv ward of Ukum LGA and Tsukwa in Tombo ward of Logo LGA. Both LGAs are located in Benue State. The attacks aﬀected 1,030 individuals and led to the displacement of 1,010 individuals to Zaki Biam in Uyam ward of Ukum LGA and Government Secondary Technical School Anyiin Camp in Mbagber ward of Logo LGA. As a result of the attacks, 20 fatalities and 36 injuries were reported.", "matched_on": "title:flash report", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": null, "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 735, "title": "Nigeria — Flood Flash Report Bauchi and Yobe States (11 October2022)", "date": "2022-10-12", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flash", "component": "Incident / Flash Report", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Bauchi", "Yobe"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-flood-flash-report-bauchi-and-yobe-states-11-october2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NE-%20Geidam%2C%20Karasuwa%20and%20Warji%20LGAs%20%2811%20October2022%29.pdf", "summary": "With the onset of the rainy season in Nigeria’s northeastern states of Yobe and Bauchi, varying degrees of damages have been reported in locations in Warji, Karasuwa and Geidam LGAs. Heavy rainfall resulted in floods and caused serious damages to shelters and infrastructure.", "matched_on": "title:flash report", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": null, "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 736, "title": "Nigeria — Emergency Tracking Tool Report 295 (26 September - 02 October 2022)", "date": "2022-10-07", "year": 2022, "component_key": "ett", "component": "Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT)", "regions": [], "states": [], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-emergency-tracking-tool-report-295-26-september-02-october-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Emergency%20Tracking%20Tool%20%28ETT%29%20Report%20No.%20295.pdf", "summary": "The DTM Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT) is deployed to track and to collect information on large and sudden population movements, provide frequent updates on the scale of displacement and quantify the aﬀected population when needed. As a sub-component of the Mobility Tracking methodology in Nigeria, ETT utilises direct observation and a broad network of key informants to capture best estimates of the aﬀected population per location, enabling targeted humanitarian response planning.", "matched_on": "title:emergency tracking tool", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-10-02", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 737, "title": "Nigeria — COVID-19 Point of Entry Monthly Dashboard (September 2022)", "date": "2022-10-07", "year": 2022, "component_key": "poe", "component": "Point of Entry (POE) Reports", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Borno"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-covid-19-point-entry-monthly-dashboard-september-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20COVID-19%20Point%20of%20Entry%20Monthly%20Dashboard%20%28September%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "During the COVID-19 pandemic, IOM's Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM), in collaboration with the World Health Organization (WHO), monitors cross-border movements to and from Nigeria's Borno State in north-east Nigeria. Assessments are conducted at Points of Entry located along the border with Cameroon.", "matched_on": "title:point of entry", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-09-01", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 738, "title": "Nigeria — North-central & North-west Flash Report 118 (03 October 2022)", "date": "2022-10-05", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flash", "component": "Incident / Flash Report", "regions": ["North Central", "North West"], "states": ["Benue"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-north-central-north-west-flash-report-118-03-october-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NCNW%20118%20%283%20October%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "On 27 September, armed herders reportedly attacked the communities Atson in North Bank II ward of Makurdi LGA and Lorjah and Chambe in Ukembergya/Tswarev ward of Logo LGA in Benue state. The attacks aﬀected 878 individuals and led to the displacement of 876 individuals to Ichwa IDP camp in North Bank I ward of Makurdi and NKST Primary School Anyiin camp and Chambe community in Mbagber ward of Logo LGA. As a result of the attacks, 2 fatalities and 18 injuries were reported. On 27, 28 and 29 September, due to the opening of the Lagdo dam in Cameroon, the river Benue overflowed and caused floods ", "matched_on": "title:flash report", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-10-03", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 739, "title": "Nigeria — Flood Flash Report Borno, Adamawa, Bauchi and Yobe States (14 - 26 September 2022)", "date": "2022-09-30", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flash", "component": "Incident / Flash Report", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Adamawa", "Bauchi", "Borno", "Yobe"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-flood-flash-report-borno-adamawa-bauchi-and-yobe-states-14-26-september-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NE%20-Borno%20Adamawa%20Bauchi%20and%20Yobe%20State%20%2814%20-%2026%20September%202022%29_0.pdf", "summary": "With the onset of the rainy season in Nigeria’s northeastern states of Borno, Adamawa, Bauchi and Yobe, varying degrees of damage have been reported in host communities, camps and camp-like settlements. Heavy rainfalls, accompanied by strong winds have resulted in floods and damage to shelters and infrastructures.", "matched_on": "title:flash report", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-09-26", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 740, "title": "Nigeria — North-central & North-west Flash Report 117  (19 - 25 September 2022)", "date": "2022-09-28", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flash", "component": "Incident / Flash Report", "regions": ["North Central", "North West"], "states": ["Benue", "Sokoto"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-north-central-north-west-flash-report-117-19-25-september-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NCNW%20117%20%2826%20September%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "On 19 September, armed bandits reportedly attacked the communities Gwandi village and Maikurfuna village in Ungushi ward of Kebbe LGA in Sokoto state. The attacks aﬀected 1,780 individuals and led to the displacement of 1,766 individuals from their respective communities to the Sobon Gari area and the UBE Tudu Wada Primary School, both situated in Kebbe East ward of Kebbe LGA. As a result of the attacks, 14 fatalities and 20 injuries were reported. On 21 and 22 September, floods resulting from an overflow of the river Benue were reported in Wadata community of Ankpa/Wadata ward in Makurdi LGA ", "matched_on": "title:flash report", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-09-25", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 741, "title": "Nigeria — Emergency Tracking Tool Report 294 (19 - 25 September 2022)", "date": "2022-09-28", "year": 2022, "component_key": "ett", "component": "Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT)", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Adamawa", "Borno"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-emergency-tracking-tool-report-294-19-25-september-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Emergency%20Tracking%20Tool%20%28ETT%29%20Report%20No.%20294.pdf", "summary": "The DTM Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT) is deployed to track and to collect information on large and sudden population movements, provide frequent updates on the scale of displacement and quantify the aﬀected population when needed. As a sub-component of the Mobility Tracking methodology in Nigeria, ETT utilises direct observation and a broad network of key informants to capture best estimates of the aﬀected population per location, enabling targeted humanitarian response planning. Between 19 and 25 September 2022, a total of 2,535 new arrivals were recorded in locations in Adamawa and Borno Sta", "matched_on": "title:emergency tracking tool", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-09-25", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 742, "title": "Nigeria — Transhumance Tracking Tool Report — Early Warning Dashboard 8 (August 2022)", "date": "2022-09-22", "year": 2022, "component_key": "ewer", "component": "Early Warning & Early Response Dashboard", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Adamawa"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-transhumance-tracking-tool-report-early-warning-dashboard-8-august-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/Nigeria%20%E2%80%94%20Transhumance%20Tracking%20Tool%20Report%20%E2%80%94%20Early%20Warning%20Dashboard%20%238%20%28August%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "In Nigeria, transhumance is an established practice among cattle herders to overcome the constraints of the dry season, diseases and conflicts in the upper Sahel region. In recent years, competing claims to natural resources have grown with reports of violent clashes between farmers’ and herders' communities in the Adamawa state of Nigeria. The conflicts between farmers and herders' communities are compounded by factors such as population growth, expanding human settlements, land privatization, year-round farming, environmental degradation, weakened traditional conflict resolving mechanisms an", "matched_on": "title:early warning dashboard", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-08-01", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 743, "title": "Nigeria — North-central & North-west Flash Report 116 (12 -18 September 2022)", "date": "2022-09-22", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flash", "component": "Incident / Flash Report", "regions": ["North Central", "North West"], "states": ["Zamfara"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-north-central-north-west-flash-report-116-12-18-september-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NCNW%20116%20%2819%20September%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "On 12 September, armed bandits reportedly attacked the communities Gidan Illo in Magaji Gari ward and Baruda in Bardoki ward. Both communities are located in Gummi LGA in Zamfara state. The attacks aﬀected 553 individuals and led to the displacement of 551 individuals from their repective communities to Government Unity School Camp in Shiyar Rafi ward, also in Gummi LGA. As a result of the attacks, 2 fatalities and 20 injuries were reported. Also, on 13 September, armed bandits reportedly attacked Duddai community in Birnin Magaji ward of Gummi LGA in Zamfara state. This attack displaced 396 i", "matched_on": "title:flash report", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-09-18", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 744, "title": "Nigeria — Emergency Tracking Tool Report 293 (12 - 18 September 2022)", "date": "2022-09-22", "year": 2022, "component_key": "ett", "component": "Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT)", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Adamawa", "Borno"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-emergency-tracking-tool-report-293-12-18-september-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Emergency%20Tracking%20Tool%20%28ETT%29%20Report%20No.%20293.pdf", "summary": "The DTM Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT) is deployed to track and to collect information on large and sudden population movements, provide frequent updates on the scale of displacement and quantify the aﬀected population when needed. As a sub-component of the Mobility Tracking methodology in Nigeria, ETT utilises direct observation and a broad network of key informants to capture best estimates of the aﬀected population per location, enabling targeted humanitarian response planning. Between 12 and 18 September 2022, a total of 1,688 new arrivals were recorded in locations in Adamawa and Borno Sta", "matched_on": "title:emergency tracking tool", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-09-18", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 745, "title": "Nigeria — Flow Monitoring Dashboard 54 (April - June 2022)", "date": "2022-09-21", "year": 2022, "component_key": "fmp", "component": "Flow Monitoring (migrants) – extra category", "regions": ["North Central", "North West"], "states": ["Niger", "Kano", "Sokoto"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-flow-monitoring-dashboard-54-april-june-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/Flow%20Monitoring%20Dashboard%2054%20June%202022.pdf", "summary": "IOM , through the Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM) Flow Monitoring tool, collects data at key entry, exit and transit points to better understand population movements across West and Central Africa . The monitoring of population flows allows for the quantification and qualification of mobility flows and trends, migrant profiles, and migratory experiences and routes. Since March 2017 two Flow Monitoring Points (FMPs) have been active in Kano and Sokoto in northern Nigeria , monitoring mobility within the country and between Nigeria, Niger and beyond.", "matched_on": "title:flow monitoring", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-06-01", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 746, "title": "Nigeria — Flood Flash Report — Bauchi State (12 September 2022)", "date": "2022-09-15", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flash", "component": "Incident / Flash Report", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Bauchi"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-flood-flash-report-bauchi-state-12-september-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NE%20-%20Ningi%2C%20Gamawa%2C%20Ganjuwa%2C%20Wargi%2C%20zaki%20and%20Damban%20LGA%20Bauchi%20State%20%2813%20September%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "A total of 2,185 individuals have been aﬀected by flooding caused by heavy rainfalls accompanied by strong winds in Bauchi State. About 90% of this total have been displaced in the LGAs Damban, Gamawa, Ganjuwa, Jama’are, Ningi, Warji and Zaki of Bauchi State  to neighboring communities. Between 01 and 12 September 2022, IOM’s DTM programme carried out  assessments to ascertain the level of damage sustained in these locations due to heavy windstorms and rainfall. Overall, 12 communities in Damban, Gamawa, Ganjuwa, Jama’are, Ningi, Warji and Zaki LGAs were assessed. The worst-hit of the assessed", "matched_on": "title:flash report", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-09-12", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 747, "title": "Nigeria — Emergency Tracking Tool Report 292 (05 — 11 September 2022)", "date": "2022-09-15", "year": 2022, "component_key": "ett", "component": "Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT)", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Adamawa", "Borno"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-emergency-tracking-tool-report-292-05-11-september-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Emergency%20Tracking%20Tool%20%28ETT%29%20Report%20No.%20292%20%281%29.pdf", "summary": "The DTM Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT) is deployed to track and to collect information on large and sudden population movements, provide frequent updates on the scale of displacement and quantify the aﬀected population when needed. As a sub-component of the Mobility Tracking methodology in Nigeria, ETT utilises direct observation and a broad network of key informants to capture best estimates of the aﬀected population per location, enabling targeted humanitarian response planning. Between 05 and 11 September 2022, a total of 1,902 new arrivals were recorded in locations in Adamawa and Borno Sta", "matched_on": "title:emergency tracking tool", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-09-11", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 748, "title": "Nigeria — North-central & North-west Flash Report 115 (12 September 2022)", "date": "2022-09-13", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flash", "component": "Incident / Flash Report", "regions": ["North Central", "North West"], "states": ["Benue"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-north-central-north-west-flash-report-115-12-september-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NCNW%20115%20%2812%20September%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "On 01 September, 32 individuals from Ortese camp in Guma LGA were displaced to New Old Market camp in Makurdi LGA of Benue State due to fear of attack. On 08 September, armed herders reportedly attacked Tse-Pevkyaa and Ortese communities in Nyiev ward and Yogbo community in Mbayer/Yendev ward of Guma LGA in Benue state. These attacks aﬀected 1,111 individuals and led to the displacement of 1,103 individuals to Daudu host community in Mbawa Council ward of Guma LGA of Benue state. Eight fatalities and 27 injuries were reported. On 09 September, flood caused by heavy rainfall was reported in the", "matched_on": "title:flash report", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-09-12", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 749, "title": "Nigeria — North-central & North-west Flash Report 114 (05 September 2022)", "date": "2022-09-12", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flash", "component": "Incident / Flash Report", "regions": ["North Central", "North West"], "states": ["Plateau", "Katsina"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-north-central-north-west-flash-report-114-05-september-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NCNW%205%20September%202022.pdf", "summary": "On 26 August, flood caused by heavy rainfall was reported in Uban Doma community in Kalong ward of Shandam LGA of Plateau state. The flood aﬀected 450 individuals, all individuals aﬀected were displaced to neighbouring shelters. On 29 August, floods caused by heavy rainfall were reported in the Sabon Unguwa, Kofar Arewa, and Marmara communities of Rimi ward of Rimi LGA and Lambobi Tudun Yanlafidda community of Katsina LGA, all in Katsina state. The floods aﬀected 765 individuals in Rimi LGA and 30 individuals in Katsina LGA. These led to displacement of 795 individuals in neighbouring shelters", "matched_on": "title:flash report", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-09-05", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 750, "title": "Nigeria — Emergency Tracking Tool Report 291 (29 August — 04 September 2022)", "date": "2022-09-12", "year": 2022, "component_key": "ett", "component": "Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT)", "regions": [], "states": [], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-emergency-tracking-tool-report-291-29-august-04-september-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Emergency%20Tracking%20Tool%20%28ETT%29%20Report%20No.%20291%20%2829%20August%20-%2004%20September%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "The DTM Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT) is deployed to track and to collect information on large and sudden population movements, provide frequent updates on the scale of displacement and quantify the aﬀected population when needed. As a sub-component of the Mobility Tracking methodology in Nigeria, ETT utilises direct observation and a broad network of key informants to capturebest estimates of the aﬀected population per location, enabling targeted humanitarian response planning.", "matched_on": "title:emergency tracking tool", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-09-04", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 751, "title": "Nigeria — Flood Flash Report — Borno, Adamawa and Yobe States (June - August 2022)", "date": "2022-09-02", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flash", "component": "Incident / Flash Report", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Adamawa", "Borno", "Yobe"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-flood-flash-report-borno-adamawa-and-yobe-states-june-august-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NE%20-Borno%2C%20Adamawa%20and%20Yobe%20Stae%20%281%20June%20-%2031%20August%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "Between June 1 and August 31 2022, IOM’s DTM programme carried out  assessments to ascertain the level of damage sustained in IDP and host community sites due to heavy windstorms, rainfall and flood. Overall, 72 host community locations, 11 camps and nine collective settlements were assessed. The worst-hit of the assessed sites was Banki, a host community location in Buduwa/Bula Chirabe ward of Bama LGA, where heavy rainfall alongside the  opening of the dam gates in Cameroon led to the flooding of the community aﬀecting an estimated 7,389 individuals. In total, 4,989 shelters/houses were dama", "matched_on": "title:flash report", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-08-01", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 752, "title": "Nigeria — Transhumance Tracking Tool Report — Early Warning Dashboard 7 (July 2022)", "date": "2022-09-01", "year": 2022, "component_key": "ewer", "component": "Early Warning & Early Response Dashboard", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Adamawa"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-transhumance-tracking-tool-report-early-warning-dashboard-7-july-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/Nigeria%20%E2%80%94%20Transhumance%20Tracking%20Tool%20Report%20%E2%80%94%20Early%20Warning%20Dashboard%207%20%28July%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "The Transhumance Tracking Tool (TTT) Early Warning System, as a component of the IOM's Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM), with support from community focal points and key informants, collects information on alerts relating to transhumance activities and movements in Adamawa state. This report presents TTT Early Warning data collected in July 2022 in five LGAs of Adamawa State (Demsa, Girei, Lamurde, Numan and Mayo-Belwa). During this period, 290 alerts were recorded, including 247 events (85%) and 43 movements (15%). Events alerts have conflict, clashes, kidnapping for ransom, cattle rustling", "matched_on": "title:early warning dashboard", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-07-01", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 753, "title": "Nigeria — Flood Flash Report — Borno State (31 August 2022)", "date": "2022-09-01", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flash", "component": "Incident / Flash Report", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Borno"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-flood-flash-report-borno-state-31-august-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NE%20-Jere%20Monguno%20and%20Kala%20Balge%20LGA%20%2831%20August%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "Between 15 and 29 August 2022, IOM’s DTM programme carried out assessments to ascertain the level of damage sustained in the sites as a result of heavy rainfall and windstorms. Overall, 11 locations in Jere, Monguno and Kala Balge LGAs were assessed. The worst-hit of the assessed sites was GGSS Camp in Monguno ward of Monguno LGA, where rainfall damaged 63 shelters, aﬀecting an estimated 1,735 individuals.", "matched_on": "title:flash report", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-08-31", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 754, "title": "Nigeria — Emergency Tracking Tool Report 290 (22 - 28 August 2022)", "date": "2022-09-01", "year": 2022, "component_key": "ett", "component": "Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT)", "regions": [], "states": [], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-emergency-tracking-tool-report-290-22-28-august-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Emergency%20Tracking%20Tool%20%28ETT%29%20Report%20No.%20290%20%2822%20-%2028%20August%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "The DTM Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT) is deployed to track and to collect information on large and sudden population movements, provide frequent updates on the scale of displacement and quantify the aﬀected population when needed. As a sub-component of the Mobility Tracking methodology in Nigeria, ETT utilises direct observation and a broad network of key informants to capture best estimates of the aﬀected population per location, enabling targeted humanitarian response planning.", "matched_on": "title:emergency tracking tool", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-08-28", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 755, "title": "Nigeria — North-central & North-west Flash Report 113 (31 August 2022)", "date": "2022-08-31", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flash", "component": "Incident / Flash Report", "regions": ["North Central", "North West"], "states": ["Sokoto"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-north-central-north-west-flash-report-113-31-august-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NCNW%20113%20%2830%20August%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "On 23 August armed bandits reportedly attacked Soron Yamma community in Soron Yamma ward in Binji LGA of Sokoto state. This attack aﬀected 315 individuals and led to the displacement of 314 individuals from Soron Yamma community to Behind Ubandoma House Gwaiwa Ekka community in Arkilla ward of Wamako LGA. In the attack, one fatality was reported and 2 individuals were injured. On 28 August, windstorm was reported in the Kofar Yandaka community of Wakilin Arewa (B) ward . The windstorm aﬀected 179 individuals and led to displacement of 178 individuals in Kofar Yandaka community to Bayan Governm", "matched_on": "title:flash report", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-08-31", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 756, "title": "Nigeria — Flood Flash Report — Adamawa State (30 August 2022)", "date": "2022-08-31", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flash", "component": "Incident / Flash Report", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Adamawa"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-flood-flash-report-adamawa-state-30-august-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NE%20-%20Numan%2C%20Lamurde%20and%20Madagali%20LGA%2C%20Adamawa%20State%20%2830%20August%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "With the onset of the rainy season in Nigeria’s northeastern state of Adamawa, varying degrees of damages have been reported in communities in the LGAs Madagali, Lamurde and Numan. Heavy rainfalls, accompanied by strong winds have caused flooding that has led to serious damages to houses and infrastructure.", "matched_on": "title:flash report", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-08-30", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 757, "title": "Nigeria — Camp Closure Flash Report — Dalori I and Dalori II, Borno State (24 August 2022)", "date": "2022-08-25", "year": 2022, "component_key": "return_intention", "component": "Return Intention & Camp Closure Reports", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Borno"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-camp-closure-flash-report-dalori-i-and-dalori-ii-borno-state-24-august-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NE%20-%20Dalori%20I%20%20II%20Camp%20Relocation%20Konduga%20LGA%20Borno%20State%20%2824%20August%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "As part of the IDP relocation programme issued by the Borno State Government (BSG), Federal Training Centre Camp (Dalori I) and 250 Housing Estate Camp (Dalori II), located in the ward Dalori of Konduga LGA were closed between 28 July 2022 and 7 August 2022. Following these events, assessments were conducted by DTM (Displacement Tracking Matrix) field staﬀ to identify the destinations of relocation of the 20,635 IDPs (4,206 households) residing in Dalori I & II, and to inform the humanitarian community. Below is a breakdown the destinations of arrival of 10,578 IDPs that are identified thus fa", "matched_on": "title:camp closure", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-08-24", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 758, "title": "Nigeria — North-central & North-west Flash Report 112 — Benue and Zamfara States (22 August 2022)", "date": "2022-08-24", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flash", "component": "Incident / Flash Report", "regions": ["North Central", "North West"], "states": ["Benue", "Zamfara"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-north-central-north-west-flash-report-112-benue-and-zamfara-states-22-august-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NCNW%20112%20%2822%20August%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "On 16 August armed bandits reportedly attacked Tudun Gyndu village in Bukkuyum ward and the villages Inligidi and Bazanjan in Adabka ward in Bukkuyum LGA of Zamfara state. These attacks aﬀected 1,035 individuals and led to the displacement of 491 individuals from Tudun Gyndu village and 543 individuals from Inligidi and Bazanjan villages to Bukkuyum Town ,the main town in Bukkuyum LGA. In the attacks, one fatality was reported and 36 individuals were injured.", "matched_on": "title:flash report", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-08-22", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 759, "title": "Nigeria — Flood Flash Report — Adamawa State (24 August 2022)", "date": "2022-08-24", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flash", "component": "Incident / Flash Report", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Adamawa"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-flood-flash-report-adamawa-state-24-august-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NE%20-%20Numan%20and%20Shelleng%20LGA%20Adamawa%20State%20%2823%20August%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "With the onset of the rainy season in Nigeria’s northeastern state of Adamawa, varying degrees of damages have been reported in communities in the LGAs Shelleng and Numan. Heavy rainfalls, accompanied by strong winds have caused flooding that has led to serious damages to shelters and infrastructures.", "matched_on": "title:flash report", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-08-24", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 760, "title": "Nigeria — Emergency Tracking Tool Report 289 (15 -21 August 2022)", "date": "2022-08-24", "year": 2022, "component_key": "ett", "component": "Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT)", "regions": [], "states": [], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-emergency-tracking-tool-report-289-15-21-august-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Emergency%20Tracking%20Tool%20%28ETT%29%20Report%20No.%20289%20%2815%20-21%20August%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "he DTM Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT) is deployed to track and to collect information on large and sudden population movements, provide frequent updates on the scale of displacement and quantify the aﬀected population when needed. As a sub-component of the Mobility Tracking methodology in Nigeria, ETT utilises direct observation and a broad network of key informants to capture best estimates of the aﬀected population per location, enabling targeted humanitarian response planning.", "matched_on": "title:emergency tracking tool", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-08-21", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 761, "title": "Nigeria — Heavy Rainfall Flash Report — Yobe State (22 August 2022)", "date": "2022-08-22", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flash", "component": "Incident / Flash Report", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Yobe"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-heavy-rainfall-flash-report-yobe-state-22-august-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NE%20-%20Gujba%20and%20Gulani%20LGA%20%2822%20August%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "With the onset of the rainy season in Nigeria’s northeastern state of Yobe, varying degrees of damages have been reported in locations of Gujba and Gulani LGAs. Rainfall, accompanied by strong winds have caused serious damages to shelters and infrastructures.", "matched_on": "title:flash report", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-08-22", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 762, "title": "Nigeria — Emergency Tracking Tool Report 288 (08 -14 August 2022)", "date": "2022-08-18", "year": 2022, "component_key": "ett", "component": "Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT)", "regions": [], "states": [], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-emergency-tracking-tool-report-288-08-14-august-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Emergency%20Tracking%20Tool%20%28ETT%29%20Report%20No.%20288%20%288%20-14%20August%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "he DTM Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT) is deployed to track and to collect information on large and sudden population movements, provide frequent updates on the scale of displacement and quantify the aﬀected population when needed. As a sub-component of the Mobility Tracking methodology in Nigeria, ETT utilises direct observation and a broad network of key informants to capture best estimates of the aﬀected population per location, enabling targeted humanitarian response planning.", "matched_on": "title:emergency tracking tool", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-08-14", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 763, "title": "Nigeria — Heavy Rainfall Flash Report — Yobe State (16 August 2022)", "date": "2022-08-16", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flash", "component": "Incident / Flash Report", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Yobe"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-heavy-rainfall-flash-report-yobe-state-16-august-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NE%20-Damaturu%20and%20Tarmua%20LGA%20%2817%20August%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "With the onset of the rainy season in Nigeria’s northeastern state of Yobe, varying degrees of damages have been reported in host communities of Tarmua and Damaturu LGAs. Heavy rainfalls, accompanied by strong winds have caused serious damages to shelters and infrastructures.", "matched_on": "title:flash report", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-08-16", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 764, "title": "Nigeria — Emergency Tracking Tool Report 287 (01 -07 August 2022)", "date": "2022-08-12", "year": 2022, "component_key": "ett", "component": "Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT)", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Adamawa", "Borno"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-emergency-tracking-tool-report-287-01-07-august-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Emergency%20Tracking%20Tool%20%28ETT%29%20Report%20No.%20287%20%2801%20-07%20August%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "Between 01 and 07 August 2022, a total of 3,843 new arrivals were recorded in Adamawa and Borno States. The new arrivals were recorded at locations in Askira/Uba, Bama, Damboa, Gwoza, Kala Balge, Monguno and Ngala Local Government Areas (LGAs) of the most conflict-aﬀected state of Borno and in Demsa, Fufore, Girei, Gombi, Hong, Lamurde, Maiha, Michika, Mubi North, Numan, Song, Yola North and Yola South LGAs of Adamawa State.", "matched_on": "title:emergency tracking tool", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-08-07", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 765, "title": "Nigeria — North-central & North-west Flash Report 110 (8 August 2022)", "date": "2022-08-11", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flash", "component": "Incident / Flash Report", "regions": ["North Central", "North West"], "states": [], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-north-central-north-west-flash-report-110-8-august-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NCNW%20110%20%288%20August%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "Nigeria's north-central and north-west zones are aﬄicted with a multi-dimensional crisis rooted in long-standing tensions between ethnic and religious groups and involves attacks by criminal groups and banditry/hirabah (such as kidnapping and grand larceny along major highways). During the past years, the crisis has accelerated because of the intensification of attacks and has resulted in widespread displacement across the region.", "matched_on": "title:flash report", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-08-08", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 766, "title": "Nigeria — North-east Dalori I Camp, Konduga LGA — Borno State Flash Report (9 August 2022)", "date": "2022-08-10", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flash", "component": "Incident / Flash Report", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Borno"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-north-east-dalori-i-camp-konduga-lga-borno-state-flash-report-9-august-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NE%20-%20Dalori%20I%20Camp%20Relocation%20Konduga%20LGA%20%28Borno%20State%29%2009%20August%202022.pdf", "summary": "As part of the IDP relocation programme issued by the Borno State Government (BSG), Federal Training Centre Camp (Dalori I), located in the ward of Dalori in Konduga LGA, was closed between 04 August 2022 and 07 August 2022. Following this event, a rapid assessment was conducted by DTM (Displacement Tracking Matrix) field staﬀ to identify the destinations of the 7,478 IDPs (1,496 households) residing in Dalori I Camp, and to inform the humanitarian community.", "matched_on": "title:flash report", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-08-09", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 767, "title": "Nigeria — Assessing the Quality of Return in North-East Nigeria (July 2022)", "date": "2022-08-10", "year": 2022, "component_key": "ses", "component": "Socio Economic Survey", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Adamawa", "Borno"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-assessing-quality-return-north-east-nigeria-july-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/Assessing%20the%20quality%20of%20return%20in%20NE%20Nigeria.pdf", "summary": "As part of its DTM programme, IOM Nigeria has incorporated a return assessment that was conducted at household level in the northeastern states of Borno and Adamawa. While new displacements continue to occur across the region, the trend of continuously increasing returnee numbers presents a major challenge to humanitarian and development actors. To assist returnees, and to facilitate a sustainable return, it is essential to measure the socio-economic profiles and needs of the returnee populations, as well as their access to services, education and participation in governance and public affairs", "matched_on": "summary:socio-economic", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-07-01", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 768, "title": "Nigeria — North-east Yobe State Flash Report (08 August 2022)", "date": "2022-08-09", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flash", "component": "Incident / Flash Report", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Yobe"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-north-east-yobe-state-flash-report-08-august-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NE%20-%20Gulani%20Gujba%20Geidam%20Machina%20and%20Bursari%20LGA%20%2808%20August%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "With the onset of the rainy season in Nigeria’s northeastern state of Yobe, varying degrees of damages have been reported in camps, camp-like settings and host communities. Heavy rainfalls, accompanied by strong winds have caused serious damages to IDP shelters and camp infrastructures.", "matched_on": "title:flash report", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-08-08", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 769, "title": "Nigeria — North-East — Mobility Tracking IDP and Returnee Atlas Round 42 (July 2022)", "date": "2022-08-09", "year": 2022, "component_key": "atlas", "component": "Mobility Tracking – IDP & Returnee Atlas", "regions": ["North East"], "states": [], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-north-east-mobility-tracking-idp-and-returnee-atlas-round-42-july-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IDP%20and%20Returnee%20Atlas%20%20%28July%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "IOM’s Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM) provides support to the Government and humanitarian partners by establishing a comprehensive system that collects, analyses and disseminates data on IDPs and returnees to ensure timely and effective assistance to the affected populations. Data collection takes place at a granular level and is repeated at regular intervals to ensure accurate and up-to-date information.", "matched_on": "file name: IDP and Returnee Atlas  (July 2022).pdf", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-07-01", "round": 42, "round_zone": "NE", "mt_main": true}, {"id": 770, "title": "Nigeria — North-east  Konduga LGA — Borno State Flash Report (5 August 2022)", "date": "2022-08-08", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flash", "component": "Incident / Flash Report", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Borno"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-north-east-konduga-lga-borno-state-flash-report-5-august-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NE%20-%20Dalori%20II%20Camp%20Relocation%20Konduga%20LGA%20%28Borno%20State%29%2005%20August%202022.pdf", "summary": "As part of the IDP relocation programme issued by the Borno State Government (BSG), 250 Housing Estate Camp (Dalori II), located in Dalori ward of Konduga LGA, was closed between 28 July 2022 and 2 August 2022. Following this event, a rapid assessment was conducted by DTM (Displacement Tracking Matrix) field staﬀ to identify the destinations of the 13,157 IDPs (2,710 households) residing in Dalori II, and to inform the humanitarian community.", "matched_on": "title:flash report", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-08-05", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 771, "title": "Nigeria — Emergency Tracking Tool Report 286 (25 - 31 July 2022)", "date": "2022-08-04", "year": 2022, "component_key": "ett", "component": "Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT)", "regions": [], "states": [], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-emergency-tracking-tool-report-286-25-31-july-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Emergency%20Tracking%20Tool%20%28ETT%29%20Report%20No.286%20%2825%20-%2031%20July%202022%29_0.pdf", "summary": "The DTM Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT) is deployed to track and to collect information on large and sudden population movements, provide frequent updates on the scale of displacement and quantify the affected population when needed. As a sub-component of the Mobility Tracking methodology in Nigeria, ETT utilises direct observation and a broad network of key informants to capture best estimates of the affected population per location, enabling targeted humanitarian response planning.", "matched_on": "title:emergency tracking tool", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-07-31", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 772, "title": "Nigeria — North-east Bama LGA Borno State Flash Report (29 July 2022)", "date": "2022-08-01", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flash", "component": "Incident / Flash Report", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Borno"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-north-east-bama-lga-borno-state-flash-report-29-july-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NE%20-%20Banki%20Camp%2C%20Bama%20LGA%2C%20Borno%20State%20%2829%20July%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "With the onset of the rainy season in Nigeria’s northeastern state of Borno, varying degrees of damages have been reported in multiple locations in the region. Heavy rainfalls, accompanied by strong winds have caused serious damages to shelters and infrastructures. On 27 July  2022, the combination of heavy rainfalls with the opening of a dam gate in Cameroon led to the flooding of the Wajare community and a large segment of Banki camp in Buduwa/Bula Chirabe ward of Bama LGA in Borno State. IOM’s DTM programme carried out an assessment to ascertain the level of damage sustained in the affected", "matched_on": "title:flash report", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-07-29", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 773, "title": "Nigeria — North-central & North-west Flash Report #108 (18 - 24 July 2022)", "date": "2022-07-29", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flash", "component": "Incident / Flash Report", "regions": ["North Central", "North West"], "states": [], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-north-central-north-west-flash-report-108-18-24-july-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NCNW%20108%20%2825%20July%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "Nigeria's north-central and north-west zones are aﬄicted with a multi-dimensional crisis rooted in long-standing tensions between ethnic and religious groups and involves attacks by criminal groups and banditry/hirabah (such as kidnapping and grand larceny along major highways). During the past years, the crisis has accelerated because of the intensification of attacks and has resulted in widespread displacement across the region.", "matched_on": "title:flash report", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-07-24", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 774, "title": "Nigeria — Emergency Tracking Tool Report 285 (18 - 24 July 2022)", "date": "2022-07-29", "year": 2022, "component_key": "ett", "component": "Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT)", "regions": [], "states": [], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-emergency-tracking-tool-report-285-18-24-july-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Emergency%20Tracking%20Tool%20%28ETT%29%20Report%20No.285%20%28%2018%20-%2024%20July%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "The DTM Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT) is deployed to track and to collect information on large and sudden population movements, provide frequent updates on the scale of displacement and quantify the affected population when needed. As a sub-component of the Mobility Tracking methodology in Nigeria, ETT utilises direct observation and a broad network of key informants to capture best estimates of the affected population per location, enabling targeted humanitarian response planning.", "matched_on": "title:emergency tracking tool", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-07-24", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 775, "title": "Nigeria — Flow Monitoring Dashboard 53 (May 2022)", "date": "2022-07-22", "year": 2022, "component_key": "fmp", "component": "Flow Monitoring (migrants) – extra category", "regions": ["North Central", "North West"], "states": ["Niger", "Kano", "Sokoto"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-flow-monitoring-dashboard-53-may-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/Flow%20Monitoring%20dashboard%2053%20May%202022.pdf", "summary": "IOM , through the Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM) Flow Monitoring tool, collects data at key entry, exit and transit points to better understand population movements across West and Central Africa . The monitoring of population flows allows for the quantification and qualification of mobility flows and trends, migrant profiles, and migratory experiences and routes. Since March 2017 two Flow Monitoring Points (FMPs) have been active in Kano and Sokoto in northern Nigeria , monitoring mobility within the country and between Nigeria, Niger and beyond.", "matched_on": "title:flow monitoring", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-05-01", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 776, "title": "Nigeria — Transhumance Tracking Tool Report — Early Warning Dashboard 6 (June 2022)", "date": "2022-07-21", "year": 2022, "component_key": "ewer", "component": "Early Warning & Early Response Dashboard", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Adamawa"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-transhumance-tracking-tool-report-early-warning-dashboard-6-june-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/Nigeria%20%E2%80%94%20Transhumance%20Tracking%20Tool%20Report%20%E2%80%94%20Early%20Warning%20Dashboard%20%236%20%28June%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "Similar to other regions in the Sahel, in the state of Adamawa, the population increase and growing numbers of livestock have resulted in the scarcity of arable land and water sources, which are essential to sustain both crop cultivation and cattle herding. The scarcity of land and water has generated farmer-herder conflicts as both communities fight for control of these resources. Encroachment by farmers on grazing land and the blockage of cattle routes have shifted the designated grazing areas and cattle passages. On the other hand, herders regularly destroy crops, pollute water sources and ", "matched_on": "title:early warning dashboard", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-06-01", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 777, "title": "Nigeria — Emergency Tracking Tool Report 284 (11 - 17 July 2022)", "date": "2022-07-21", "year": 2022, "component_key": "ett", "component": "Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT)", "regions": [], "states": [], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-emergency-tracking-tool-report-284-11-17-july-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Emergency%20Tracking%20Tool%20%28ETT%29%20Report%20No.284%20%28%2011%20-%2017%20July%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "The DTM Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT) is deployed to track and to collect information on large and sudden population movements, provide frequent updates on the scale of displacement and quantify the affected population when needed. As a sub-component of the Mobility Tracking methodology in Nigeria, ETT utilises direct observation and a broad network of key informants to capture best estimates of the affected population per location, enabling targeted humanitarian response planning.", "matched_on": "title:emergency tracking tool", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-07-17", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 778, "title": "Nigeria — North-east Song LGA Adamawa State Flash Report (19 July 2022)", "date": "2022-07-19", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flash", "component": "Incident / Flash Report", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Adamawa"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-north-east-song-lga-adamawa-state-flash-report-19-july-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NE%20-%20Song%20LGA%20Flood%20Adamawa%20State%20%2819%20July%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "With the onset of the rainy season in Nigeria’s northeastern state of Adamawa, varying degrees of damages have been reported in multiple locations in the region. Heavy rainfalls, accompanied by strong winds have caused serious damages to shelters and infrastructures. On 17 July  2022, heavy rainfalls in Song LGA in Adamawa State resulted in the flooding of the Loko communities in the ward Song Gari. IOM’s DTM programme carried out assessments to ascertain the level of damage sustained in the affected communities. Over 1,200 individuals from 148 households were displaced from Song Gari Ward in ", "matched_on": "title:flash report", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-07-19", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 779, "title": "Nigeria — Emergency Tracking Tool Report 283 (04 - 10 July 2022)", "date": "2022-07-14", "year": 2022, "component_key": "ett", "component": "Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT)", "regions": [], "states": [], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-emergency-tracking-tool-report-283-04-10-july-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Emergency%20Tracking%20Tool%20%28ETT%29%20Report%20No.283%20%2804%20-%2010%20July%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "The DTM Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT) is deployed to track and to collect information on large and sudden population movements, provide frequent updates on the scale of displacement and quantify the affected population when needed. As a sub-component of the Mobility Tracking methodology in Nigeria, ETT utilises direct observation and a broad network of key informants to capture best estimates of the affected population per location, enabling targeted humanitarian response planning.", "matched_on": "title:emergency tracking tool", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-07-10", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 780, "title": "Nigeria — North-east — Displacement Report 41 (June 2022)", "date": "2022-07-13", "year": 2022, "component_key": "atlas", "component": "Mobility Tracking – IDP & Returnee Atlas", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Adamawa", "Bauchi", "Borno", "Gombe", "Taraba", "Yobe"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-north-east-displacement-report-41-june-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/DTM%20Report%20Round%2041%20%20%28June%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "This report, which presents the results from Round 41 of Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM) assessments carried out by the International Organization for Migration (IOM), aims to improve the understanding of the scope of internal displacement and return movements in north-east Nigeria. The report covers the period from 14 February to 30 March 2022 and reflects the trends from the six states in Nigeria’s north-east geopolitical zone. This zone is the most affected by the conflict and consists of the following states: Adamawa, Bauchi, Borno, Gombe, Taraba and Yobe.", "matched_on": "inside PDF: “LACEMENT REPORT | ROUND 41 IOM DISPLACEMENT TRACKING MATRIX BASELINE ASSESSMENT IN NORTH-EAST NIGERIA 24% Women 19% Men ”", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-06-01", "round": 41, "round_zone": "NE", "mt_main": true}, {"id": 781, "title": "Nigeria — North-east Jere and Maiduguri M. C. LGAs Borno State Flash Report (08 July 2022)", "date": "2022-07-08", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flash", "component": "Incident / Flash Report", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Borno"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-north-east-jere-and-maiduguri-m-c-lgas-borno-state-flash-report-08-july-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NE%20-%20Maiduguri%20M.C%20and%20Jere%20LGAs%20Windstorm%20%28Borno%20State%29%20-%20%2808%20July%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "With the onset of the rainy season in Nigeria’s northeastern state of Borno, varying degrees of damages have been reported in camps and camp-like settings. Heavy rainfalls, accompanied by strong winds have caused serious damages to IDP shelters and camp infrastructures.", "matched_on": "title:flash report", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-07-08", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 782, "title": "Nigeria — Emergency Tracking Tool Report 282 (27 June - 03 July 2022)", "date": "2022-07-08", "year": 2022, "component_key": "ett", "component": "Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT)", "regions": [], "states": [], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-emergency-tracking-tool-report-282-27-june-03-july-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Emergency%20Tracking%20Tool%20%28ETT%29%20Report%20No.282.pdf", "summary": "The DTM Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT) is deployed to track and to collect information on large and13 sudden population movements, provide frequent updates on the scale of displacement and quantify the affected population when needed. As a sub-component of the Mobility Tracking methodology in Nigeria, ETT utilises direct observation and a broad network of key informants to capture best estimates of the affected population per location, enabling targeted humanitarian response planning.", "matched_on": "title:emergency tracking tool", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-07-03", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 783, "title": "Nigeria — North-central & North-west Flash Report 107 (27 June - 03 July 2022)", "date": "2022-07-07", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flash", "component": "Incident / Flash Report", "regions": ["North Central", "North West"], "states": [], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-north-central-north-west-flash-report-107-27-june-03-july-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NCNW%20107%20%284%20July%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "Nigeria's north-central and north-west zones are aﬄicted with a multi-dimensional crisis rooted in long-standing tensions between ethnic and religious groups and involves attacks by criminal groups and banditry/hirabah (such as kidnapping and grand larceny along major highways). During the past years, the crisis has accelerated because of the intensification of attacks and has resulted in widespread displacement across the region.", "matched_on": "title:flash report", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-07-03", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 784, "title": "Nigeria — COVID-19 Point of Entry Monthly Dashboard (June 2022)", "date": "2022-07-06", "year": 2022, "component_key": "poe", "component": "Point of Entry (POE) Reports", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Borno"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-covid-19-point-entry-monthly-dashboard-june-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20COVID-19%20Point%20of%20Entry%20Monthly%20Dashboard%20%28June%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "During the COVID-19 pandemic, IOM's Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM), in collaboration with the World Health Organization (WHO), monitors cross-border movements to and from Nigeria's Borno State in north-east Nigeria. Assessments are conducted at Points of Entry located along the border with Cameroon.", "matched_on": "title:point of entry", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-06-01", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 785, "title": "Nigeria — Flow Monitoring Dashboard 52 (April 2022)", "date": "2022-07-01", "year": 2022, "component_key": "fmp", "component": "Flow Monitoring (migrants) – extra category", "regions": ["North Central", "North West"], "states": ["Niger", "Kano", "Sokoto"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-flow-monitoring-dashboard-52-april-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/Flow%20Monitoring%20Dashboard%2052%20April%202022.pdf", "summary": "IOM , through the Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM) Flow Monitoring tool, collects data at key entry, exit and transit points to better understand population movements across West and Central Africa . The monitoring of population flows allows for the quantification and qualification mobility flows and trends, migrant profiles, and migratory experiences and routes. Since March 2017 two Flow Monitoring Points (FMPs) have been active in Kano and Sokoto in northern Nigeria , monitoring mobility within the country and between Nigeria, Niger and beyond.", "matched_on": "title:flow monitoring", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-04-01", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 786, "title": "Nigeria — Emergency Tracking Tool Report 281 (20 - 26 June 2022)", "date": "2022-07-01", "year": 2022, "component_key": "ett", "component": "Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT)", "regions": [], "states": [], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-emergency-tracking-tool-report-281-20-26-june-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Emergency%20Tracking%20Tool%20%28ETT%29%20Report%20No.281_0.pdf", "summary": "The DTM Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT) is deployed to track and to collect information on large and sudden population movements, provide frequent updates on the scale of displacement and quantify the affected population when needed. As a sub-component of the Mobility Tracking methodology in Nigeria, ETT utilises direct observation and a broad network of key informants to capture best estimates of the affected population per location, enabling targeted humanitarian response planning.", "matched_on": "title:emergency tracking tool", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-06-26", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 787, "title": "Nigeria — North-east Madagali LGA, Adamawa State Flash Report (27 June 2022)", "date": "2022-06-29", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flash", "component": "Incident / Flash Report", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Adamawa"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-north-east-madagali-lga-adamawa-state-flash-report-27-june-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NE%20-%20Madagali%20Adamawa%20State%20%2828%20June%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "The lingering conflict in Nigeria's North East Zone has been the major cause of widespread population displacement. Over 2 million persons have been forced to leave their areas of residence in search of safety and security in neighbouring wards and LGAs.", "matched_on": "title:flash report", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-06-27", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 788, "title": "Nigeria — North-central & North-west Flash Report #106 (20 - 26 June 2022)", "date": "2022-06-29", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flash", "component": "Incident / Flash Report", "regions": ["North Central", "North West"], "states": [], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-north-central-north-west-flash-report-106-20-26-june-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NCNW%20106%20%2827%20June%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "Nigeria's north-central and north-west zones are aﬄicted with a multi-dimensional crisis rooted in long-standing tensions between ethnic and religious groups and involves attacks by criminal groups and banditry/hirabah (such as kidnapping and grand larceny along major highways). During the past years, the crisis has accelerated because of the intensification of attacks and has resulted in widespread displacement across the region.", "matched_on": "title:flash report", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-06-26", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 789, "title": "Nigeria — Emergency Tracking Tool Report 280 (13 - 19 June 2022)", "date": "2022-06-24", "year": 2022, "component_key": "ett", "component": "Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT)", "regions": [], "states": [], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-emergency-tracking-tool-report-280-13-19-june-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Emergency%20Tracking%20Tool%20%28ETT%29%20Report%20No.280%20%2813%20-%2019%20June%202022%29_1.pdf", "summary": "The DTM Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT) is deployed to track and collect information on large and sudden population movements, provide frequent updates on the scale of displacement and quantify the affected population when needed. As a sub-component of the Mobility Tracking methodology in Nigeria, ETT utilises direct observation and a broad network of key informants to capture best estimates of the affected population per location, enabling targeted humanitarian response planning.", "matched_on": "title:emergency tracking tool", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-06-19", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 790, "title": "Nigeria — North-east Adamawa and Gombe States Flash Report (22 June 2022)", "date": "2022-06-22", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flash", "component": "Incident / Flash Report", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Adamawa", "Gombe"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-north-east-adamawa-and-gombe-states-flash-report-22-june-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NE%20-%20Lamurde%20Guyuk%20and%20Balanga%20LGA%28Adamawa%20and%20Gombe%29%20communal%20clash%2022%20June%202022.pdf", "summary": "Surging communal violence between ethnic and religious groups, and long-standing conflicts between farming communities and with nomadic herders are prevalent across north-east Nigeria. These conflicts are predominantly centered on disputes over land and cause great insecurity and widespread displacement across the region.", "matched_on": "title:flash report", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-06-22", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 791, "title": "Nigeria — North-central & North-west Flash Report #105 (06 - 11 June 2022)", "date": "2022-06-22", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flash", "component": "Incident / Flash Report", "regions": ["North Central", "North West"], "states": [], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-north-central-north-west-flash-report-105-06-11-june-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NCNW%20104%20%2821%20June%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "Nigeria's north-central and north-west zones are afflicted with a multi-dimensional crisis rooted in long-standing tensions between ethnic and religious groups and involves attacks by criminal groups and banditry/hirabah (such as kidnapping and grand larceny along major highways). During the past years, the crisis has accelerated because of the intensification of attacks and has resulted in widespread displacement across the region.", "matched_on": "title:flash report", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-06-11", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 792, "title": "Nigeria — North-East — Displacement Factsheet 41 (14 February - 30 March 2022)", "date": "2022-06-22", "year": 2022, "component_key": "atlas", "component": "Mobility Tracking – IDP & Returnee Atlas", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Adamawa", "Bauchi", "Borno", "Gombe", "Taraba", "Yobe"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-north-east-displacement-factsheet-41-14-february-30-march-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/Round%2041%20-%20Factsheet_0.pdf", "summary": "This report, which presents the results from Round 41 of Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM) assessments carried out by the International Organization for Migration (IOM), aims to improve the understanding of the scope of internal displacement and return movements in north-east Nigeria. The report covers the period from 14 February to 30 March 2022 and reflects the trends from the six states in Nigeria’s north-east geopolitical zone. This zone is the most affected by the conflict and consists of the following states: Adamawa, Bauchi, Borno, Gombe, Taraba and Yobe.", "matched_on": "title:displacement factsheet", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-03-30", "round": 41, "round_zone": "NE", "mt_main": null}, {"id": 793, "title": "Nigeria — Flow Monitoring Dashboard 51 (March 2022)", "date": "2022-06-21", "year": 2022, "component_key": "fmp", "component": "Flow Monitoring (migrants) – extra category", "regions": [], "states": [], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-flow-monitoring-dashboard-51-march-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/Flow%20Monitoring%20Dashboard%2051%20March%202022.pdf", "summary": "In order to gain a better understanding of mobility flows and trends throughout West and Central Africa, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) implements the Displacement Tracking Matrix’s Flow Monitoring (FM) tool at key transit points across the region. Flow Monitoring activities are conducted in close cooperation with national and local authorities as well as with local partners. The Flow Monitoring tool consists of two main components: the Flow Monitoring Registry (FMR), which captures key data on the magnitude, provenance, destination and mode of travel of mobility flows, and", "matched_on": "title:flow monitoring", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-03-01", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 794, "title": "Nigeria — COVID-19 Point of Entry Dashboard 109 (11 — 17 June 2022)", "date": "2022-06-21", "year": 2022, "component_key": "poe", "component": "Point of Entry (POE) Reports", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Borno"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-covid-19-point-entry-dashboard-109-11-17-june-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20COVID-19%20Point%20of%20Entry%20Dashboard%20109%20%2811-17%20June%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "During the COVID-19 pandemic, IOM's Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM), in collaboration with the World Health Organization (WHO), monitors cross-border movements to and from Nigeria's Borno State in north-east Nigeria. Assessments are conducted at Points of Entry located along the border with Cameroon.", "matched_on": "title:point of entry", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-06-17", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 795, "title": "Nigeria — Emergency Tracking Tool Report 279 (06 - 12 June 2022)", "date": "2022-06-17", "year": 2022, "component_key": "ett", "component": "Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT)", "regions": [], "states": [], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-emergency-tracking-tool-report-279-06-12-june-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Emergency%20Tracking%20Tool%20%28ETT%29%20Report%20No.279%20%2806%20-%2012%20June%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "The DTM Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT) is deployed to track and to collect information on large and sudden population movements, provide frequent updates on the scale of displacement and quantify the affected population when needed. As a sub-component of the Mobility Tracking methodology in Nigeria, ETT utilises direct observation and a broad network of key informants to capture best estimates of the affected population per location, enabling targeted humanitarian response planning.", "matched_on": "title:emergency tracking tool", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-06-12", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 796, "title": "Nigeria — Transhumance Tracking Tool Report — Early Warning Dashboard 5 (May 2022)", "date": "2022-06-16", "year": 2022, "component_key": "ewer", "component": "Early Warning & Early Response Dashboard", "regions": [], "states": [], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-transhumance-tracking-tool-report-early-warning-dashboard-5-may-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/Nigeria%20%E2%80%94%20Transhumance%20Tracking%20Tool%20Report%20%E2%80%94%20Early%20Warning%20%235%20%28May%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "Farmers-Herdsmen conflicts are propelled by multi-causal factors, such as limited resources in the face of population increment and its attendant increment of needs, weakened traditional conflict resolving mechanisms and shortage of land, and climate change. These narratives and profiles have aided aggressive encroachment and reprisal aggression between the parties leading to mutual hostility and reverse-violent attacks. Further, tensions have grown with reports of violent clashes becoming more frequent, and in recent years, disputes over crop damage, livestock theft, and water pollution have ", "matched_on": "title:early warning dashboard", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-05-01", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 797, "title": "Nigeria — COVID-19 Point of Entry Dashboard 108 (04 — 10 June 2022)", "date": "2022-06-14", "year": 2022, "component_key": "poe", "component": "Point of Entry (POE) Reports", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Borno"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-covid-19-point-entry-dashboard-108-04-10-june-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20COVID-19%20Point%20of%20Entry%20Dashboard%20%2804%20-10%20June%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "During the COVID-19 pandemic, IOM's Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM), in collaboration with the World Health Organization (WHO), monitors cross-border movements to and from Nigeria's Borno State in north-east Nigeria. Assessments are conducted at Points of Entry located along the border with Cameroon.", "matched_on": "title:point of entry", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-06-10", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 798, "title": "Nigeria — North-east Guyuk and Lamurde LGA — (Adamawa State) Flash Report 10 June 2022", "date": "2022-06-10", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flash", "component": "Incident / Flash Report", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Adamawa"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-north-east-guyuk-and-lamurde-lga-adamawa-state-flash-report-10-june-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NE%20-%20Lamurde%20and%20Guyuk%20LGA%20Adamawa%20State%20Communal%20Clash%20report%2010%20June%202022.pdf", "summary": "Surging communal violence between ethnic and religious groups, and long-standing conflicts between farming communities and with nomadic herders are prevalent across north-east Nigeria. These conflicts are predominantly centered on disputes over land and cause great insecurity and widespread displacement across the region.", "matched_on": "title:flash report", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-06-10", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 799, "title": "Nigeria — Emergency Tracking Tool Report 278 (30 May - 05 June 2022)", "date": "2022-06-10", "year": 2022, "component_key": "ett", "component": "Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT)", "regions": [], "states": [], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-emergency-tracking-tool-report-278-30-may-05-june-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Emergency%20Tracking%20Tool%20%28ETT%29%20Report%20No.278%20%2830%20May%20-%2005%20June%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "The DTM Emergency Tracking Tool (ETT) is deployed to track and to collect information on large and13 sudden population movements, provide frequent updates on the scale of displacement and quantify the affected population when needed. As a sub-component of the Mobility Tracking methodology in Nigeria, ETT utilises direct observation and a broad network of key informants to capture best estimates of the affected population per location, enabling targeted humanitarian response planning.", "matched_on": "title:emergency tracking tool", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-06-05", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 800, "title": "Nigeria — North-central & North-west Flash Report #103 (30 May - 05 June 2022)", "date": "2022-06-08", "year": 2022, "component_key": "flash", "component": "Incident / Flash Report", "regions": ["North Central", "North West"], "states": [], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-north-central-north-west-flash-report-103-30-may-05-june-2022", "pdf": "https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/IOM%20Nigeria%20DTM%20Flash%20Report%20NCNW%20103%20%287%20June%202022%29.pdf", "summary": "Nigeria's north-central and north-west zones are afflicted with a multidimensional crisis rooted in long-standing tensions between ethnic and religious groups and involves attacks by criminal groups and banditry/hirabah (such as kidnapping and grand larceny along major highways). During the past years, the crisis has accelerated because of the intensification of attacks and has resulted in widespread displacement across the region. Between the 30th of May and 5th of June 2022, armed clashes and banditry have led to new waves of population displacement. Following these events, rapid assessments", "matched_on": "title:flash report", "date_basis": "publication date", "period_date": "2022-06-05", "round": null, "round_zone": null, "mt_main": null}, {"id": 801, "title": "Nigeria — COVID-19 Point of Entry Dashboard 107 (28 May — 03 June 2022)", "date": "2022-06-07", "year": 2022, "component_key": "poe", "component": "Point of Entry (POE) Reports", "regions": ["North East"], "states": ["Borno"], "url": "https://dtm.iom.int/reports/nigeria-covid-19-point-entry-dashboard-10